 ## Overview
-Position Map Voxelization is a post-processing step that reads a 2D position map containing world-space positions of surface fragments and writes active voxel indicators into a 3D volume texture [S1, unofficial]. It marks the primary voxel and its 8 immediate neighbors as active to ensure connectivity or fill gaps [S1, unofficial]. It differs from direct rasterization methods by decoupling surface identification from volume population, allowing for gap-filling connectivity via neighbor marking [S1, unofficial].
